WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:19.251
"Now what do we do?" Cole asked, staring after the mystery man.

2
00:00:19.252 --> 00:00:21.437
"Do you think he's the culprit?"

3
00:00:21.438 --> 00:00:24.529
Maggie frowned. "I don't get it.

4
00:00:24.530 --> 00:00:29.951
Nobody here knows him. Why would some stranger slash our tires?"

5
00:00:29.952 --> 00:00:34.593
"People get robbed by strangers all the time," Cole pointed out.

6
00:00:34.594 --> 00:00:37.273
"That's different," Henry said.

7
00:00:37.274 --> 00:00:42.674
"Robbers have a motive. They want the money or other stuff that they steal.

8
00:00:42.675 --> 00:00:46.486
What's that guy's motive for slashing our tires?"

9
00:00:46.487 --> 00:00:50.794
"I don't know," Cole said. "But I think the new tires are here."

10
00:00:50.795 --> 00:00:53.160
A van was pulling into the field.

11
00:00:53.161 --> 00:00:58.976
It had the Belltown Bikes logo painted on the side.

12
00:00:58.977 --> 00:01:07.515
Several of the bike shop's employees jumped out and started helping people replace their tires.

13
00:01:07.516 --> 00:01:11.465
Before long all the bikes were fixed.

14
00:01:11.466 --> 00:01:16.518
Ms. Hernandez made the riders line up so she could make sure everyone was there.

15
00:01:16.519 --> 00:01:22.136
Then she got on her bike. "Time to get back on the trail!" she called out.

16
00:01:22.137 --> 00:01:30.231
"Hip, hip, hooray!" Melanie cheered, jumping up and down. "Go, Belltown!"

17
00:01:30.232 --> 00:01:32.714
Soon Henry was back on the trail.

18
00:01:32.715 --> 00:01:35.561
But he wasn't paying attention to the scenery.

19
00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:38.400
He was still thinking about the mystery.

20
00:01:38.401 --> 00:01:43.217
"We need to keep working on this case," he told Maggie and Cole.

21
00:01:43.218 --> 00:01:48.346
"Why?" Maggie asked. "That mystery man probably did it.

22
00:01:48.347 --> 00:01:51.943
Why else would he lie to us about being a newspaper reporter?"

23
00:01:51.944 --> 00:01:56.996
"I don't know," Henry said. "He might have other reasons."

24
00:01:56.997 --> 00:02:01.227
Cole nodded. "Yeah. Maybe he's a spy!"

25
00:02:01.228 --> 00:02:02.852
Henry doubted that.

26
00:02:02.853 --> 00:02:07.273
But he had a feeling The Lemonade Detectives were missing an important clue.

27
00:02:07.274 --> 00:02:10.985
"Let's split up and talk to people again," he said.

28
00:02:10.986 --> 00:02:20.543
"If we can prove everybody else didn't do it, we can investigate that mystery man."

29
00:02:20.544 --> 00:02:26.919
They spent the next few minutes talking to people as they rode along.

30
00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:31.243
Henry questioned different riders about what they'd seen during the break.

31
00:02:31.244 --> 00:02:36.150
The more he learned, the more he realized that most riders had alibis.

32
00:02:36.151 --> 00:02:41.229
Either they hadn't left the picnic area, or they'd been with other people when they had.

33
00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:44.011
Then he caught up to William.

34
00:02:44.012 --> 00:02:49.683
"I guess Ms. Hernandez talked him out of quitting," he thought.

35
00:02:49.684 --> 00:02:53.824
"Hi, William," Henry called. "Are you having fun?"

36
00:02:53.825 --> 00:02:58.148
William looked over at him. "Sure, I guess so."

37
00:02:58.149 --> 00:03:03.873
"Good," Henry said. "Because I heard you talking to Ms. Hernandez earlier.

38
00:03:03.874 --> 00:03:07.171
Why did you want to quit partway through the ride?"

39
00:03:07.172 --> 00:03:09.889
William looked surprised and then annoyed.

40
00:03:09.890 --> 00:03:15.550
"None of your business," he muttered. Then he sped up and rode off.

41
00:03:15.551 --> 00:03:18.876
His fancy mountain bike could go really fast.

42
00:03:18.877 --> 00:03:23.400
Henry was wondering whether he should try to catch up when he heard Maggie.

43
00:03:23.401 --> 00:03:25.517
"Henry! Wait up!"

44
00:03:25.518 --> 00:03:28.976
A second later she and Cole both caught up to him.

45
00:03:28.977 --> 00:03:31.899
The three of them discussed what they'd found out.

46
00:03:31.900 --> 00:03:38.549
"It seems like there are only five people who don't have alibis for the time of the crime," Henry said.

47
00:03:38.550 --> 00:03:44.205
"Nathan, Ms. Hernandez, Tina, William, and the mystery man."

48
00:03:44.206 --> 00:03:48.960
"We know Nathan would never slash people's tires," Cole said.

49
00:03:48.961 --> 00:03:54.112
Henry nodded. "I think we can cross Ms. Hernandez off the list too.

50
00:03:54.113 --> 00:03:59.643
That leaves three suspects: Tina, William, and the mystery man."

51
00:03:59.644 --> 00:04:02.870
"I still think Tina did it," Cole said.

52
00:04:02.871 --> 00:04:08.635
"Why would she come on the ride to raise money for Belltown High unless she wanted to cause trouble?"

53
00:04:08.636 --> 00:04:14.051
"I don't know," Henry said. "But we can't assume it was her.

54
00:04:14.052 --> 00:04:18.009
We thought it was Joey, and he had an alibi, remember?"

55
00:04:18.010 --> 00:04:20.513
He rode around a curve in the trail.

56
00:04:20.514 --> 00:04:26.695
He was thinking so hard, it took him a second to spot the rider stopped by the side of the trail.

57
00:04:26.696 --> 00:04:31.374
It was Nathan. He was standing beside his bike, looking worried.

58
00:04:31.375 --> 00:04:37.388
The Lemonade Detectives stopped beside him. "What's wrong?" Maggie asked.

59
00:04:37.389 --> 00:04:41.397
"It's my bike." Nathan pointed toward the gears.

60
00:04:41.398 --> 00:04:46.765
"The chain fell off! And I don't know how to fix it. Can you guys help?"

61
00:04:46.766 --> 00:04:50.897
Henry shook his head. "I don't know how to fix it either."

62
00:04:50.898 --> 00:04:54.436
He looked at Maggie and Cole. "What about you two?"

63
00:04:54.437 --> 00:04:57.021
They shook their heads too.

64
00:04:57.022 --> 00:05:02.162
"Maybe you can leave your bike here and ride double with one of us," Maggie suggested.

65
00:05:02.163 --> 00:05:06.942
Just then Joey rode toward them. He smirked when he saw them.

66
00:05:06.943 --> 00:05:14.419
"Having bike trouble, Belltown losers?" he yelled. "Good, you deserve it!"

67
00:05:14.420 --> 00:05:19.592
He sped around the next curve, making dirt fly at them as he passed.

68
00:05:19.593 --> 00:05:23.498
"Go back to Valley High, you bully!" Maggie yelled.

69
00:05:23.499 --> 00:05:29.393
"Forget about him." Nathan sighed. "What am I going to do about my bike?"

70
00:05:29.394 --> 00:05:32.167
A few more riders rounded the curve.

71
00:05:32.168 --> 00:05:38.851
Some of them looked over at Nathan's broken bike. But nobody stopped.

72
00:05:38.852 --> 00:05:41.019
Then Tina rode into view.

73
00:05:41.020 --> 00:05:46.345
As soon as she saw Nathan's bike, she steered toward him.

74
00:05:46.346 --> 00:05:50.228
"Your chain fell off, huh?" she said with a friendly smile.

75
00:05:50.229 --> 00:05:56.691
"Don't worry. I can help you fix it."
